            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A circuit (11) configured to debounce a signal (IN1) is disclosed. An input node is configured to receive an input signal (IN1). A timer circuit is configured to be started in response to an edge being detected in the input signal (IN1) and be stopped after a debouncing time interval having a certain duration. An output node is configured to produce an output signal (IN1'). The circuit (11) is configured to pass the input signal (IN1) from the input node to the output node while the timer circuit is not running, and to prevent the output signal (IN1') from changing value while the timer circuit is running. The circuit (11) further includes an adaptation circuit (110) configured to receive a clock signal (CLK), measure (111) a period of the clock signal (CLK), and set (114) the duration of the debouncing time interval as a function of the measured period of the clock signal (CLK).</p>
            </abstract>
